WEBVTT

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.920
Training camp starts today!

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.730
Tenma.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:16.800
It looks like you're in for some difficulties, but for you, things will work out somehow!

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:17.620
Right?

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.600
I think so too!

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.750
Then work hard out there and win, Captain!

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.800
Okay! I'll be going now!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.750
I'll go do my best, Sasuke!

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.860
This is the new soccer hall.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.150
Other than this stadium, there's also a boardinghouse prepared for us.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.410
Tenma!

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.410
I-I'm sorry!

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.580
I'm okay, I'm okay.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:27.720
Captain!

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.020
G-Good morning!

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.970
Morning.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.040
You're here early! Were you practicing?

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.350
Yes.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.750
Everyone else is already here.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.050
Wow, you're right!

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:44.960
They're just not practicing real practice.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.400
Why did Coach choose them...

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.980
This is great!

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.520
Good morning, everyone!

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.570
I'm surprised you're all here so early!

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.610
Let's work well together!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:08.290
We will be holding training camp here for the week before FFI Vision 2's Asia preliminaries begin.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.920
Let's begin with self-introductions.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.670
Matatagi, you first.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:15.720
Yes, sir.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.650
Matatagi Hayato.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.010
I was in the track club.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.470
Track? Which event?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.470
Sprinting.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.470
I see! No wonder you're so fast!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.870
I'm Nozaki Sakura!

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.670
I do rhythmic gymnastics.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.420
Rhythmic gymnastics?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.650
What?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.670
I'm Tetsukado Shin.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.860
I was a boxer.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.570
Kusaka Ryuuji.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.500
I did nothing in particular.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.250
Nothing?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.800
No sports or anything?

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:49.830
That's right.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.820
I'm Ibuki Munemasa.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.040
I play basketball.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.630
Yeah, you're the goalkeeper.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.880
Manabe Jin'ichirou.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.350
This is my first time playing soccer, but it won't be a problem.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.720
I'll be a pro at it almost immediately.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.770
I'm Minaho Kazuto.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.950
From what I've seen so far, it appears that I will be the brains of this team.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.270
Any background in soccer?

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.570
None.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.650
I guess I'm what you call a beginner?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.670
Then you're no different from me-

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.240
Last person!

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.320
I-I'm Morimura Konoha...

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.220
And? Have you played soccer before?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.870
Trainer!

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.460
On what grounds were these members chosen?!

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:39.950
No grounds, they're who Coach Kuroiwa selected.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.000
I don't know why either.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.220
But whatever the reason, you eleven here are Inazuma Japan.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.750
Coach!

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.670
Let me introduce you to this team's manager.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.900
I'm Mizukawa Minori.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.770
Manager?

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.780
What school is she from?

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.400
And the other one.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.270
Come in.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.620
Yes, sir!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.970
I'm manager of Raimon's soccer club, Sorano Aoi!

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.290
I've been recently appointed manager for New Inazuma Japan.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:21.750
Aoi!

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.720
When did this happen?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.770
I had no idea!

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.170
I got a sudden call about it today!

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.050
I'm surprised myself!

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.370
I see.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.720
Let's do our best!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.320
Yeah!

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.600
Be best in the world, you hear?

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.700
Yeah!

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.870
All I desire from Inazuma Japan is victory.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.650
That is all you may expect from me.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:49.780
Matsukaze.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:51.520
Yes, sir!

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:56.250
Let's start by building up the endurance we need for soccer.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.720
Since we have to keep running during the match, stamina is very important...

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:08.950
Going through the basics isn't a bad idea, but wouldn't it be better practicing hissatsu techniques first?

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.500
That seems much more practical.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.570
There are some people here who haven't played sports before.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.520
Basic training for now is important.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:24.020
Also, hissatsu techniques are only made after the individual player has developed and fortified their specialty.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.030
It won't happen right away.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.200
I've already completed my hissatsu technique...

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.030
...in here.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.700
Okay.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.020
But today is our first day of practice.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.250
I want us to work on strength-building first for what's to come.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.500
You got it.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.000
Then let's all go running.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.700
Give it all you've got!

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:06.220
They're all relatively serious about their training.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:11.950
Break time!

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.820
We're going to use the ball next, so rest up!

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.170
Matatagi!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.300
It's break time! Take a rest!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.070
I'm still okay with running some more.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.820
Soccer is different from marathons. Pacing yourself is important.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.570
I know that...

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.600
But I like running.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.100
I see.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.570
So do I!

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:45.670
Being paired up with you makes me feel like doing better, so I keep speeding up every time.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:48.280
Maybe this will bring out a new hissatsu technique.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.780
Is that how hissatsu techniques are made?

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:54.220
It depends on the person though.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:57.920
I want to improve more, too, for the world tournament.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:02.270
If we can make a new hissatsu technique with that speed, it would be thanks to you, Matatagi.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.700
That's the type of guy I can't trust the most.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:21.950
You might find it inconvenient how you can't use your hands, but once you get used to the ball, you'll be able to control it rather easily.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.420
Try it, everyone!

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:48.670
Damn it!

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.000
That's it for today's practice.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.820
My, my, my, it's a pleasure to meet you, a pleasure to meet you.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.650
Just look at all that sweat and dirt on you.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:20.000
A bath, you definitely need to take a bath first.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Oh, but your rooms before that, your rooms!

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.700
Leave your bags in your rooms before you go shower.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.670
U-Um... our rooms?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.670
It's written on that bulletin board.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.090
Kamata-san runs this place. She's a fun person, isn't she?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.650
Everyone calls her Auntie.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.220
Tenma.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.920
After you've put down your bag, come with me.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:48.000
O-Okay.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.370
I wonder what Shinsuke is doing now...

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.450
The match is in one week.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.000
There's no time.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:12.170
Watching the three boys from Raimon is such fun.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.300
Is that so.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:16.820
Particularly their irritation.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.340
Thus, leading to...

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.920
Coach.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.300
Please redo your selection for the team.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:26.770
This team won't win!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.820
My decision is final.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:35.550
I want you three to bring out their potential.

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:37.470
Their potential?

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.650
Just why do you hold such a high opinion of them?

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.750
As if he would give us a straight answer.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.740
If you're that bent on your decision, Coach...

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.220
Then the three of us will win the matches to come on our own!

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.090
Just the three of you, eh?

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.900
Tsurugi will be forward.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.270
Tenma will be midfielder.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.200
And I will play defense.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:02.050
When the other team shoots, I will block them!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.900
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.450
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:26.950
Do as you please.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.670
Shindou-san, by the three of us, you don't really mean...?

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.850
That Coach is desecrating soccer!

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.250
Cut the crap!

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.420
You, block the shoots?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.470
I'm Japan's goalkeeper!

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.050
Ibuki...

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.450
Don't flatter yourself.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.170
You're a complete beginner.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.500
That's why I'm here to practice!

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.050
Tsurugi, practice with me!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.000
Ibuki!

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.150
Okay.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.020
No, I'll shoot.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:01.030
If you can't stop my shoot, then you could never stop Tsurugi's.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.370
All right.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.870
Try one of those hissatsu shoots on me.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.000
Fortissimo!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.750
I gave you what you wanted.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.220
Nice. Give me more!

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:34.810
Matatagi...

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.520
What did you think about today's training?

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:48.070
I'm not sure if what I've learned in track can be applied here or not...

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.950
But I'm getting an idea of what my role is in this team.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:53.900
Role?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.920
I'll break through the opponent's formation with my running.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.300
I see.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.250
You're right.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.850
You only need to look at the goal in track.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:05.550
But soccer is different.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:08.150
There are so many things you need to keep an eye on.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.260
I'm still not used to that.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:14.970
I could only do dribbling at first.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:18.060
All I could look at were my feet and the ball.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:23.650
But after I joined Raimon and met Shindou-san and Tsurugi, I learned to see so much.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.750
Then I started loving soccer even more!

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:31.320
When you grow to love it, soccer answers back to that love!

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:33.500
The way to get better at something is to love doing it!

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:35.460
I see.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:36.720
Yeah!

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.650
Let's keep doing our best tomorrow.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:40.450
Okay.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:46.590
Your first opponent for the Asia preliminaries is Korea's Fire Dragon.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:50.550
According to our info, the team's cornerstone is their forward, Lee Chun-yoon.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:55.310
He is an extremely fast runner, and once he has the ball, it's over.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.870
He brings it up to the goal before anyone can stop him.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.520
An extremely fast runner...

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:04.820
The only way is to keep Chun-yoon from getting the ball.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.550
Both defense and offense will be given their relevant training menus for this purpose.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:08.070
Understood?

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.280
Yes, sir!

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.870
All right! I got past Captain!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:19.820
Good job! That's the way.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.700
You're improving, Matatagi.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:23.770
Here I go!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.770
You won't get through me!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:31.470
That was very clumsy.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.260
Your right leg was off by an angle of more than 5 degrees.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:34.800
What's more...

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:37.250
Sorry, sorry.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:49.240
One more time!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:03.960
Not bad.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.000
Now it's my turn!

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:12.720
Hayato-niichan!

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:16.370
Matatagi-kun, you have visitors!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.180
Hey!

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:19.180
Yuuta! Shun!　{雄太 瞬}

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.550
Nii-chan!

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.950
We're here to watch you practice!

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.550
I've gotten pretty good at soccer.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.270
Really?!

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.910
Something like that.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.670
Wow, that's so cool!

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:37.120
That's awesome, Nii-chan!

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.370
Hello!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:43.750
Your brother worked really hard to get this good.

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:47.170
Will you come cheer for him in our match against Korea?

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:48.570
Yeah, we'll go!

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:49.620
We'll definitely be there!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.320
I'll see you later.

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.320
Nii-chan, Nii-chan.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:56.100
What?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.800
Compared to you, none of the other guys here seem like much of a big deal.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.450
Dummy, don't say that.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.150
What if someone heard you?

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.950
For adults, it's important to preserve how relationships look on the surface.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:08.860
Got that?

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.360
Yeah, we know!

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.360
A week has passed.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.320
The Asia preliminaries are tomorrow.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.870
To be honest, we can't rely on the other members.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.830
The three of us will have to handle it ourselves.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.710
But they've all really improved-

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.170
But not at a level where they can challenge the world.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:33.750
This is the best choice we can make if we want to win.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:39.650
But this past week, while I watched Matatagi and the others, I felt something from them.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:42.730
I can sense something fierce inside of them like we do.

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:45.600
I sense nothing.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.800
This day has come at last!

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:58.170
Football Frontier International Vision 2's Asia preliminaries!

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:01.470
I, Kakuma Oushou, will provide you with the commentary!

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:09.270
Which team will win these prelims to bear the honor of representing Asia?!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:11.470
Nii-chan!

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.500
You can do it!

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:21.320
After the opening ceremony, the first match between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Korea's Fire Dragon will begin!

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.020
Shindou-san!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:27.150
What?

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.820
U-Um...

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.750
They're not powerful enough, but...

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:35.700
I think we should fight with these members as a team after all!

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:41.750
Raimon practiced so hard to be chosen as representatives until we bled!

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:43.570
Don't you understand, Tenma?!

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.750
This is the world tournament!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:51.170
If we fight this match with everything we've got, I'm sure the others will follow us!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.710
I just don't think these members were chosen for no reason!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.400
Tenma!

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.020
Tenma, come with me!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:12.420
You're the only one among us who would steal it, Matatagi-kun.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.920
Is it true your wallet is missing?

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:16.800
Yes.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.100
He says he hasn't forgotten it back at the boardinghouse either.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:22.070
But that doesn't mean you should suspect Matatagi!

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:28.920
I've heard that Matatagi-kun was once caught stealing in the past.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:33.590
So you're the only one here likely enough to steal my wallet.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.210
I didn't do it.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.570
Minaho-kun, what do you think?

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.670
We need conclusive evidence.

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:45.500
We don't even have circumstantial evidence at the moment.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:48.320
Your reasoning is still rather faulty.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.150
Just whose side are you on?!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:50.650
But-

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.110
Stop it! We have a game to play!

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:57.920
We are representative players! Everyone has their expectations in us!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.490
So we need to fight in a way that won't cause embarrassment, and win!

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:08.200
But none of us are here because we wanted to play soccer.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:13.220
Each of us was hired under certain terms.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.670
Hired?

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:22.120
For instance, Tetsukado-kun comes from a family of fishermen and he is earning the money to repair their broken fishing boat.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:27.070
Nozaki-san is here so she can study abroad in the world's best rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:31.100
Even Ibuki-kun is here to cover the costs of studying abroad in an overseas basketball team, is that correct?

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.060
Yeah.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.570
No way...

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.450
Is that true?

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:40.070
Matatagi, is that true for you too?

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:47.020
I... want to buy a big house for my family to live in.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.300
No way...

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.080
Unbelievable...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.950
I want a clear response from you here.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:20:00.170
You aren't leading Japan's team to defeat because of some scheme, are you?

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:08.350
Like receiving a bribe from agents in other countries, for instance, and purposely forming a weak team.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:12.350
That's the rumor floating around.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.230
Let them say what they want.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:22.970
Both teams for Japan and Korea in this first match have taken their positions!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:28.070
I can feel the players' boiling fighting spirit even from here!

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.820
The match will begin momentarily!

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:32.200
Inazuma Japan against Fire Dragon!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:34.450
There's the fated kickoff!

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.820
Give it back to me right away.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:39.920
Matatagi!

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.470
Matatagi!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.220
Stop them!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:54.190
You won't get through!

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:58.190
Guys! Remember our training!

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:00.950
He's coming!

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.170
Don't stand in front of me!

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.000
Lee Chun-yoon is fast!

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.160
He's already in front of the goal!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.660
I'll stop it-

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.910
Shindou-san!

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:24.070
Inazuma Japan!

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:27.120
We'll score the first point!

00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:55.970
The first round of the Asia preliminaries!

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:58.560
We're playing against Korea's representatives, Fire Dragon!

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.920
The result of that rollercoaster match is...?

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:03.100
Next, A Small Change!

00:23:03.100 --> 00:23:05.020
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:19.450
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:25.250
The way to get better at something is to love doing it!

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:26.370
That's all!
